1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,830
[GORD PIKE] GORD: Can't sleep, Drizzle?

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,580
PREVIOUSLY: DAY 1

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:08,140
A supply run. An explosion. An empty spot.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,990
By dusk, the smoke over Dale's still hadn't stopped.

5
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:19,410
DRIZZLE: They've been gone six hours.

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,750
MAGS: Five and a half. I'm counting.

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,270
Four went down the hill. Three came back.

8
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,500
[WES PRUITT · Cal's twin] WES: Cal? Where's Cal?

9
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,600
GORD: He was right behind us. Right behind us.

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,150
[ROY · back from Dale's] ROY: He wasn't behind us, Gord.

11
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:44,790
Nobody said anything. Everybody looked at Gord.

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,140
GORD: The wire sparked. The whole place went up.

13
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,560
GORD: Cal ran out the back. He'll turn up.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,630
[DANA REYES · back from Dale's] DANA: You told him to grab the water first.

15
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:00,240
GORD: I told everyone to get OUT.

16
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:06,140
Two stories. One missing man. And it was getting dark.

17
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,490
WES: Then I'm going down there.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,210
GORD: Nobody goes down in the dark.

19
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,670
WES: That's my BROTHER.

20
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:17,370
MAGS: First light. With a buddy. Not alone.

21
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:22,070
DRIZZLE: First-aid kit, it's in my— oh.

22
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:26,950
MAGS: Cool water. Not ice. Ten minutes, at least.

23
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:30,260
MAGS: And that ring comes off before it swells.

24
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:32,040
ROY: That's our drinking water.

25
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:34,230
MAGS: Then we drink less tonight.

26
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:38,140
BURNS: COOL RUNNING WATER, 10+ MINUTES. NO ICE.

27
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:41,890
[BENNY OCHOA] BENNY: Butter. My grandma swore by it.

28
00:01:42,010 --> 00:01:43,930
MAGS: Your grandma was wrong.

29
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,320
DRIZZLE: We've got nothing to wrap it with.

30
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,590
[DARLA FINCH] DARLA: What ELSE is in that bag?

31
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:56,000
COVER LOOSELY WITH A CLEAN DRESSING. DON'T POP BLISTERS.

32
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:00,100
DRIZZLE: Okay. Everybody find a buddy. Say their name.

33
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,200
After a disaster, the first job is knowing who's here.

34
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,740
MAGS: Dale? ...Still missing.

35
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:09,150
MAGS: Cal Pruitt?

36
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:16,000
COUNT EVERYONE. WRITE IT DOWN. NOBODY GOES ANYWHERE ALONE.

37
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,630
DARLA: Drizzle's bag went missing while they were gone.

38
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,720
DARLA: So who stayed up here?

39
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:26,270
[LYLE KEMPER] LYLE: She won't open hers. Why not?

40
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,150
GORD: Good question.

41
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,290
GORD: Open the bag, Tess.

42
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,490
[TESS VARGA] TESS: It's not his bag. And it's not yours.

43
00:02:38,610 --> 00:02:43,720
DRIZZLE: Hers has a padlock. Mine didn't. Mine was... a snack bag.

44
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:47,520
MAGS: Pointing fingers in the dark is how camps fall apart.

45
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:49,610
GORD: Then who took it, Drizzle?

46
00:02:49,730 --> 00:02:51,950
DRIZZLE: ...I don't know. Yet.

47
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:56,570
The rain got colder. And everyone was wet.

48
00:02:56,690 --> 00:03:00,730
MAGS: He's soaked through. Wet clothes off, dry on.

49
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:04,980
DRIZZLE: I'd give him my slicker, but... it's kind of my whole thing.

50
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:08,200
MAGS: Then get him off the ground. And a hat.

51
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,140
HYPOTHERMIA: GET DRY. INSULATE FROM THE GROUND. COVER THE HEAD.

52
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,970
[HANK DORSEY] HANK: Here. This'll warm him up.

53
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:18,750
MAGS: No. Alcohol makes you lose heat faster.

54
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:22,310
MAGS: Warm and sweet. And huddle up.

55
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,240
TESS: ...Thank you.

56
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:30,000
WARM SWEET DRINKS. SHARE BODY HEAT. NEVER ALCOHOL.

57
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,960
WES: Three blinks. Cal and I did it as kids.

58
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,470
WES: It means 'I'm okay.'

59
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:44,130
Far below, a light blinked back.

60
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,900
WES: ...Only twice.

61
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:52,920
GORD: Lights out. Save your batteries. Water's locked up with me.

62
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,850
Gord kept the water case in his own tent.

63
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:59,170
MAGS: 'With me.' Remember he said that.

64
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:04,990
DRIZZLE: Cool water for burns. Count everyone. Stay dry.

65
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,220
DRIZZLE: And trust... carefully?

66
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:12,210
MAGS: Someone took your bag while we all watched the smoke.

67
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,390
MAGS: Not everyone on Gord's side went down the hill.

68
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,760
[MILO VARGA] MILO: Psst. Drizzle.

69
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,890
MILO: I saw where your snack bag went.

70
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:26,150
DRIZZLE: You... what?

71
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:29,830
MILO: Lyle carried it. While the smoke was going.

72
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:33,010
MILO: He put it in the big tent. That one.

73
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:38,140
Drizzle had prepared for an earthquake. Not for this.

74
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,410
DRIZZLE: That's... that's my bag.

75
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,690
And under it, the water everyone else was rationing.

76
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,180
DRIZZLE: Milo, stay behind me.

77
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,830
GORD: Can't sleep, Drizzle?

78
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:57,170
GORD: Keeping it safe. Keeping the peace.

79
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:00,600
DRIZZLE: The first-aid kit was in it. Roy needed it.
